# DigiSwasthya Product Definition Document — Part 21: Canvas-Derived Feature Specifications (Addendum)

## Purpose of this Part

The design canvases (`DigiSwasthya.dc.html`, `PharmacyPanel.dc.html`, `StockistPanel.dc.html`, `PlatformAdmin.dc.html`) contain features and flows that are not specified in Parts 1–20. By product decision (2026-07-31), **every such feature is in scope** and must exist in the application. This Part specifies each of them completely, in product terms.

Rules of this Part:

1. Parts 1–20 prevail on conflict. Where a canvas behaviour contradicted an established rule (for example, a stockist creating orders invisibly, or an open public marketplace), the feature is **adapted** here so that it delivers the canvas capability without breaking the rules. Nothing is dropped.
2. Features that require real external services (SMS/email gateways, payment gateways, OCR, artificial intelligence, mapping APIs, multi-device synchronisation) are specified with a **local platform equivalence**: a deterministic, fully local behaviour that delivers the same user value in this system.
3. Every feature here is normative for the build, exactly like Parts 1–20.
4. Feature identifiers are CF-01 … CF-39 (CF-38 is intentionally unassigned). Notification codes introduced here are N-301 … N-316. Edge cases are E-CF-*. These extend, and never renumber, the existing catalogues.
5. All eight product principles apply unchanged, in particular: **orders, invoices and payments remain the only financial truth** (every ledger, commission or analytics view in this Part is derived and read-only), **accuracy over automation** (no assisted feature ever commits a business action by itself), and **verification before trade**.

