# SECTION B — STOCKIST FEATURES

## CF-11 Manual Order on Behalf of a Pharmacy

**Purpose.** The canvas stockist "New Order": record an order that a connected pharmacy placed by phone/WhatsApp — without violating the rule that pharmacies own their purchase decisions.

**Actors & permissions.** New permission `order.recordManual`: Stockist Owner, Manager. Requires an Active connection with the pharmacy.

**Behaviour.**
1. The stockist picks a connected pharmacy, then enters lines by product picker or text quick-entry (CF-02 parser over the stockist's own active catalogue).
2. Saving creates a normal Order with `source = Manual` and `createdBy = stockist`, in status **Pending**, priced by current PTR snapshot, MOQ enforced.
3. The pharmacy is **notified immediately** (N-303) and sees the order in its own Orders list, clearly badged "Recorded by stockist", with its normal Pending-order rights (including Cancel).
4. From Pending onward the standard order lifecycle (Part 9) applies unchanged — the stockist accepts/fulfils it like any other order.

**Rules & validations.** Manual orders are impossible without an Active connection; they respect all catalogue/stock/pricing rules; the source and creator are permanently visible on the order for both parties and in audit.

**Notifications.** N-303 "Order recorded on your behalf" → pharmacy users (plus the existing order lifecycle notifications thereafter).

**Edge cases.** E-CF-11a: pharmacy cancels a Manual order → same as any Pending cancellation, stockist notified. E-CF-11b: stockist may not record a Manual order for a suspended pharmacy (blocked with the standard suspension error).

## CF-12 Partner Invite ("Add Pharmacy", adapted)

**Purpose.** The canvas "Add Pharmacy" without letting stockists create pharmacy records: invite off-platform pharmacies to register and connect.

**Actors & permissions.** Stockist Owner, Manager (`partner.invite`).

**Behaviour.** The stockist enters pharmacy name + phone (and optional email/GST). If a business with that GST/phone already exists on the platform, the system deep-links to the existing connection flow instead. Otherwise it creates a tracked invite (`Sent`) and produces a shareable registration message/link. When a business later registers matching the invite's phone/GST, the invite becomes `Registered`; when a connection between the pair becomes Active, `Connected`.

**Rules.** No business or user records are created by the invite itself; registration is always performed by the pharmacy (Part 2 flows).

**Notifications.** N-304 "Invited pharmacy joined" → the inviting stockist (on Registered).

**Edge cases.** E-CF-12a: duplicate invite to the same phone → the existing invite is shown, not duplicated. E-CF-12b: invites never expire silently; they can be withdrawn.

## CF-13 Offline Payment Recording ("Record Payment" / "Mark Paid", adapted)

**Purpose.** Record remittances that happened outside the platform (cash handed over, direct UPI), preserving dual-entry visibility.

**Actors & permissions.** New permission `payment.recordOffline`: Stockist Owner, Accountant, Manager.

**Behaviour.**
1. From an invoice (shortcut "Mark paid" prefills the outstanding amount) or from a pharmacy's page, the stockist records: amount, mode (Cash/UPI/NEFT/Cheque), reference, date, optional proof file, allocation to one or more of **that pharmacy's** open invoices.
2. This creates a normal Payment with `recordedBy = Stockist` in status **Submitted**. The pharmacy is notified at once (N-305) and sees the payment in its own history, permanently badged "Recorded by stockist".
3. The stockist then approves it through the standard review step (self-approval allowed here, but the record and audit trail permanently show who recorded and who approved). All standard payment rules apply: allocation ≤ outstanding, duplicate-reference detection, immutability after approval.

**Rules.** This never bypasses the payment state machine; outstanding amounts change only on approval, exactly as for pharmacy-submitted payments.

**Notifications.** N-305 "Payment recorded on your account" → pharmacy users; existing approval/rejection notifications thereafter.

**Edge cases.** E-CF-13a: pharmacy disputes a recorded payment → it raises a support ticket referencing the payment (Part N flows); the payment itself remains immutable. E-CF-13b: duplicate reference across recorded and submitted payments is flagged identically.

## CF-14 Payment Reminders

**Purpose.** Canvas "Send Reminder" on receivables.

**Actors & permissions.** Stockist Owner, Manager, Accountant (`reminder.send`).

**Behaviour.** From an overdue/outstanding invoice or a pharmacy row, "Send reminder" issues an in-app notification to the pharmacy (N-307) and optionally posts a templated line into the pair's message thread ("Payment reminder: INV-…, ₹… due since …"). Reminders are logged (who, when, for what).

**Rules.** Throttle: at most one reminder per invoice per day. Reminders never change any document state (messages never approve anything — Part 1 principle).

**Edge case.** E-CF-14a: reminder on a fully settled invoice is blocked with an explanatory error.

## CF-15 QR on Bill + Bill Verification

**Purpose.** Canvas QR/verify-bill: any invoice can be verified as genuine on this platform installation.

**Actors & permissions.** QR appears on every issued invoice document. Verification is public (no login).

**Behaviour.**
1. Every issued invoice carries a QR encoding: invoice number, stockist name, pharmacy name, grand total, issue date, and an integrity code computed from the invoice's immutable fields.
2. A public verification screen accepts a scanned/pasted payload and answers exactly one of: **Genuine** (all fields match the stored invoice — summary shown), **Mismatch** (invoice exists but a field differs — differing fields named), **Not found**.

**Rules.** Verification is read-only and reveals only the summary fields already on the printed bill. Voided invoices verify as "Genuine — VOIDED" with the void date.

**Notifications.** None.

**Edge cases.** E-CF-15a: tampered amount → Mismatch naming the amount. E-CF-15b: QR from another installation (unknown invoice) → Not found, with the explanation that verification is per-installation.

**Local platform equivalence.** Verification checks the local data store; there is no central server. The integrity code is a deterministic hash of the immutable invoice fields.

## CF-16 Bulk Bill Generation

**Purpose.** Canvas bulk billing: issue many invoices at once.

**Actors & permissions.** `invoice.issue` roles (Owner, Manager, Accountant).

**Behaviour.** A queue lists fulfilment-ready orders without invoices (Packed, or per billing policy). The user multi-selects and issues invoices in one action; the system processes each order independently (one invoice per order — the existing one-invoice rule is unchanged) and reports per-order success/failure (partial success semantics, Part 16 error category 9).

**Edge case.** E-CF-16a: an order that gains an invoice between listing and execution fails its row with the standard duplicate-invoice error; the rest proceed.

## CF-17 Supplier Procurement (Stockist's Own Purchasing)

**Purpose.** The canvas procurement suite (Suppliers, Purchase Orders, Purchases/GRN, Bill History, Required Stock, Manufacturer Returns, bill entry wizard) — the stockist's upstream supply management. Suppliers are the stockist's local records; they are **not platform participants**.

**Actors & permissions.** New permissions `supplier.manage`, `po.manage`: Stockist Owner, Manager (Staff may receive stock).

**Behaviour.**
1. **Suppliers:** CRUD records (name, contact, GST optional, notes). Deletion only when no open POs; otherwise deactivate.
2. **Purchase Orders:** created from scratch, from the Required-Stock view (low-stock products prefill a draft), or via text quick-entry (CF-02 parser over the stockist's own catalogue). Lines: product, quantity, expected cost. Lifecycle: `Draft → Sent → PartiallyReceived → Received → Closed`, `Cancelled` from Draft/Sent.
3. **Receiving:** against a Sent/PartiallyReceived PO, the user records received lines (quantity, batch number, expiry, cost). Receiving **creates/updates inventory batches through the standard stock-in path**, writing inventory movements with the PO as source document. Over-receipt beyond ordered quantity requires explicit confirmation.
4. **Purchase Bills:** supplier bill records (bill number, supplier, date, amount, optional file attachment, link to PO(s)). A quick-entry form allows pasting bill text to prefill lines (parser; OCR simulated).
5. **Manufacturer/Supplier Returns:** select own batches (typically near-expiry/expired/damaged), quantities, supplier, reason. Lifecycle `Draft → Sent → Settled` (or Cancelled from Draft). Sending decrements stock with movements; settlement records the credit/replacement note text.
6. **Required Stock:** a view of products at/below reorder level with suggested order quantities feeding PO drafts.

**Rules.** Platform trade documents (Parts 3–10) are never touched by procurement records; the only shared effect is inventory, always via movements. Expired stock cannot be received into sellable state (it lands as Expired).

**Notifications.** N-308 "Purchase order fully received" → stockist users (informational).

**Edge cases.** E-CF-17a: receiving a batch number that already exists for the product adds to that batch only if expiry matches, otherwise requires a distinct batch number. E-CF-17b: cancelling a PartiallyReceived PO is blocked (close it instead). E-CF-17c: supplier return of quantity exceeding current on-hand is blocked.

**Local platform equivalence.** No supplier connectivity: POs are records the stockist communicates outside the platform; "OCR" is the text parser.

## CF-18 Delivery Routes & Scheduling (Stockist)

**Purpose.** Canvas routes/route-execution/scheduling for the stockist's own dispatches.

**Actors & permissions.** `route.manage`: Owner, Manager. Delivery Boys execute stops assigned to them.

**Behaviour.**
1. Routes: name, coverage (areas/PINs), default assignee, ordered stops. Deliveries (Part 9 H-series) can be assigned to a route and sequenced.
2. Route execution view (for the assignee): ordered stops with pharmacy name, address, phone, the delivery's documents, per-stop actions Delivered / Failed (existing delivery state machine; reasons required on failure), and an external-map deep-link per address.
3. **Scheduling:** dispatch may set a scheduled delivery date; the pharmacy sees it on the order (notification N-316). Rescheduling re-notifies.
4. **Delivery fee (optional):** a stockist-level rule (flat fee and/or free-above-threshold) may add a visible delivery-charge line to invoices at issue time. The fee is part of the invoice like any other line and follows invoice immutability.

**Rules.** Route mechanics never alter delivery/state rules; a route is an organisational layer over existing deliveries.

**Notifications.** N-316 "Delivery scheduled/rescheduled" → pharmacy users.

**Edge cases.** E-CF-18a: unassigned route stop cannot be executed. E-CF-18b: fee rule changes never affect already-issued invoices.

## CF-19 Business Holidays (Stockist)

**Purpose.** Canvas holidays management.

**Behaviour.** Stockist maintains a list of holiday dates with labels. They display on the stockist's profile/detail as seen by pharmacies, and the pharmacy checkout shows an informational banner when the stockist is closed on/around the requested delivery date.

**Rules.** Holidays never block ordering (informational only).

## CF-20 Price History

**Purpose.** Canvas price-history view.

**Behaviour.** Every product price change (single edit or bulk update) writes a price-change record (product, old→new PTR/MRP, who, when, source: manual/bulk/import). A history view lists changes filterable by product/date; the product detail shows its own trail. Existing rule preserved: historical order/invoice prices never change.

**Notifications.** Existing price-change notification to connected pharmacies applies (one per change batch, not per row).

## CF-21 Public Catalogue Share

**Purpose.** Canvas share-catalogue link/QR.

**Behaviour.** The stockist can open/share a read-only catalogue view: business identity, product list with pack size and MRP. **PTR and stock quantities are never included** (Part 7 privacy). The share view carries a "become a customer" prompt pointing to registration/connection.

**Local platform equivalence.** The link is a local route usable for demonstration on the same installation; QR encodes that route.

