# SECTION C — PLATFORM ADMINISTRATION FEATURES

## CF-22 Commission Monitor & Transactions View

**Purpose.** Canvas admin Money/Commission/Transactions — as **derived, read-only monitoring** (Part 19 excludes commission as product truth; this feature is analytics over real documents).

**Actors & permissions.** Platform Admin, SuperAdmin (`read.platform`); configuration `settings.manage` (SuperAdmin).

**Behaviour.**
1. **Configuration:** a platform commission rate (percentage of invoice grand total), with optional per-stockist overrides.
2. **Commission ledger (derived):** computed from non-void issued invoices — per period and per stockist: invoice count, invoice value, computed commission. Exportable. Clearly labelled: "Derived monitoring view. Invoices are the source of truth. No amounts are collected or owed through this system."
3. **Transactions view:** a read-only, filterable register of all payments and invoices platform-wide, with anomaly flags: duplicate payment references, businesses with duplicate-GST candidates, unusually large payments (> configurable multiple of the pair's average). Flags link to the underlying documents and to the involved businesses.

**Rules.** Zero write paths to any financial document from these screens.

**Notifications.** None.

**Edge cases.** E-CF-22a: changing the rate re-computes displays only; nothing retroactive is stored per invoice. E-CF-22b: ledger totals must reconcile exactly with the invoice register for the same filters.

## CF-23 Premium Plans & Upgrade Requests

**Purpose.** Canvas Upgrade/Premium — as a local, admin-approved plan system.

**Actors & permissions.** Business Owner requests; Platform Admin/SuperAdmin decides; plan copy managed under `plan.manage` (SuperAdmin).

**Behaviour.**
1. Plans page (per business): current plan (default Free), Premium benefits list, price text.
2. Upgrade request: the business submits a payment declaration — UPI reference/UTR (required) + proof screenshot (optional file). Status `Submitted`.
3. Admin queue: review request (business, UTR, proof) → Approve (business becomes Premium, badge shown; premium-flagged conveniences unlock, e.g. saved report presets) or Reject with reason (business may resubmit).
4. Admin may also revoke Premium with reason (audited).

**Rules.** Plan state never affects trade rules, pricing, or financial documents — conveniences only. The declared UTR is a text record; no gateway is called.

**Notifications.** N-309 upgrade requested → admins; N-310 decision → business users.

**Edge cases.** E-CF-23a: one open request per business. E-CF-23b: duplicate UTR across requests is flagged to the reviewing admin.

## CF-24 Counterfeit Management

**Purpose.** Canvas counterfeit module: report suspicious product/batch, investigate, and act — wired to the existing batch-recall machinery.

**Actors & permissions.** Reporting: pharmacy or stockist users (`ticket.create`-equivalent, new action `counterfeit.report`). Handling: Platform Admin/SuperAdmin (`counterfeit.review`).

**Behaviour.**
1. A report captures: product (and batch if known), seller (if relevant), description, optional evidence files.
2. Admin queue: `Reported → Investigating` (assignee, internal notes) → outcome: **Issue Recall** (marks the identified batch(es) Recalled via the standard batch state machine; all businesses holding or supplied from the batch are notified), **Dismiss** (reason), or **Resolve** (note) after a recall completes.
3. The reporter can see their report's status; all steps are audited.

**States.** `Reported → Investigating → RecallIssued → Resolved`, or `Investigating → Dismissed`.

**Notifications.** N-311 report filed → admins; N-313 batch recall notice → affected businesses; N-314 report outcome → reporter.

**Edge cases.** E-CF-24a: recall on a batch with open (reserved) allocations → reservations released and affected orders flagged to the stockist. E-CF-24b: duplicate reports on one batch are linked to a single investigation.

## CF-25 Impersonation ("Log in as", read-only)

**Purpose.** Canvas admin "Log in as" — with hard safety guarantees.

**Actors & permissions.** SuperAdmin only (`impersonate`).

**Behaviour.**
1. From a business detail page, "View as business" requires a reason, then opens that business's portal **in read-only mode**: a persistent banner shows "Viewing <business> as Platform Support — read-only", and every mutating action is disabled and blocked.
2. Entering and exiting impersonation writes audit entries (admin, business, reason, timestamps). "Exit" returns to the admin portal.
3. Optionally (default on), the business owner is notified that platform support viewed their workspace (N-315).

**Rules.** Zero mutations are possible while impersonating — enforced at the service layer, not just visually. Impersonation never reveals user passwords or session secrets.

**Edge cases.** E-CF-25a: impersonating a suspended business shows its read-only portal with the suspension banner. E-CF-25b: concurrent impersonation sessions are not allowed (one at a time).

## CF-26 Reports Hubs

**Purpose.** Canvas report tiles for every portal — canned, filtered CSV exports built from local data.

**Behaviour.**
- **Admin:** registrations over time; verification throughput (submitted/approved/rejected, average days); GMV by month (invoice-based); ticket volume & resolution; commission summary (CF-22).
- **Pharmacy:** purchases by period/supplier; GST summary (input tax from invoices, using each invoice's tax split); stock aging (inventory by expiry band); outstanding by supplier.
- **Stockist:** sales by period/pharmacy; GST summary (output tax); outstanding & aging by pharmacy; stock aging & value at risk.
Every export includes the generation timestamp and the filter summary in the file. Export actions respect the export permission rules (Part 13) and are audited.

