# SECTION D — SHARED SHELL FEATURES

## CF-27 Help Center

**Purpose.** Canvas Help & Support hub in every portal.

**Behaviour.** Per portal: FAQ accordion (platform FAQ content, role-relevant subset), short "how do I…" guides for the core journeys of that role (connect, order, receive, pay / fulfil, invoice, collect / verify, govern), a contact card (platform support identity), a link to raise/see support tickets, and a "Replay walkthrough" action (CF-28).

**Rules.** Help content is static platform content, versioned with the app; it never gives business advice.

## CF-28 Onboarding Walkthrough

**Purpose.** Canvas first-login walkthrough.

**Behaviour.** On a user's first login per role, a 4-step walkthrough presents that role's core loop and where things live; it can be skipped, never blocks, is remembered per user, and can be replayed from Help/Settings.

## CF-29 Global Search

**Purpose.** Canvas topbar search, and Part 5 "search relevant data".

**Behaviour.** A global search in the shell finds, within the actor's permitted scope: documents by number (orders, invoices, payments, returns, credit notes, deliveries, tickets), products by name/SKU, trading partners by name, and app pages by name. Selecting a result navigates to it. Results never include another business's private data.

**Edge case.** E-CF-29a: number-shaped queries (e.g. `INV-…`) prioritise exact document matches.

## CF-30 Preferences & Settings Toggles

**Purpose.** Canvas settings switches, made real.

**Behaviour.**
1. **Notification preferences** per user: non-critical notification categories can be muted (critical/action-required categories cannot). The fan-out honours mutes.
2. **Appearance:** light (default, unchanged) / dark theme toggle. The default look is exactly today's.
3. **Language:** selector with English active; the copy architecture supports future languages (no hidden hard-coded strings in new code).
4. **Local-first indicator:** informational toggle controlling the "data stored locally in this browser" hint; the application is local-first by design (Part 17's connectivity behaviour applies only to future remote features).
5. **Session panel:** shows current session start, business, role; "sign out". (Multi-device session management is out of scope — single-installation platform.)
6. **Workspace data:** export/import of the full local workspace (already specified) — must always include every table this Part adds.

## CF-31 Profile Menu & Sign-out Confirmation

**Behaviour.** The shell shows a profile menu (user name, role, business) with Profile, Settings, Help, and Sign out (with confirmation). Available in all portals, desktop and mobile.

## CF-32 Dashboard Interaction Parity

**Purpose.** The canvases' dashboard ergonomics, uniformly.

**Behaviour.**
1. Every dashboard KPI/queue card is **actionable**: it deep-links to the corresponding list pre-filtered to exactly the counted set (or opens a detail modal where a list does not exist).
2. "Today's Work" tiles per role: the role's actionable queues (e.g. pharmacy: to receive, to pay, low stock; stockist: to accept, to pack, to dispatch, payments to review; admin: verifications, tickets).
3. Quick-action grids per role (new order/sale, add product, stock in, invite staff, etc. — each a link to the existing flow).
4. After completing a major action (order placed, GRN saved, payment submitted/approved, invoice issued), a success summary presents the created document number and the natural next actions.
5. Setup checklists per role on the dashboard until completed (pharmacy: verify → connect → order → pay; stockist: verify → catalogue → stock → fulfil).

