# SECTION E — SUPPLEMENTARY FEATURES

## CF-33 Stock Transfer Between Own Locations (Stockist)

**Purpose.** Canvas stock-transfer screen — moving stock between the stockist's own storage points, without full multi-warehouse complexity.

**Actors & permissions.** Stockist Owner, Manager (`inventory.adjust`).

**Behaviour.** The stockist maintains a simple list of its own location labels (e.g. Main Warehouse, Branch Depot). A transfer selects: from-location, to-location (must differ), product/batch, quantity (> 0, ≤ on-hand at source). The transfer writes paired `TransferOut`/`TransferIn` inventory movements referencing each other. Sellable totals are unchanged; the location label is informational on batch records.

**Rules.** Transfers never change total sellable quantity and never touch reserved stock. This is locations-lite — allocation/fulfilment logic remains location-agnostic (full multi-warehouse remains a Part 19 future item; this feature only delivers the canvas capability of recording internal moves).

**Edge case.** E-CF-33a: transferring more than un-reserved on-hand at the source is blocked.

## CF-34 Role Preview (Owner Tool)

**Purpose.** Canvas "Preview as role" — let an Owner see the portal as a given role would, to understand permissions.

**Actors & permissions.** Business Owner only.

**Behaviour.** A preview selector applies another role's UI gating (nav trimming, hidden actions) to the Owner's own session, with a visible "Previewing as {role}" banner and one-click exit. Preview affects **presentation only**: any action the Owner performs is still executed and audited as the Owner.

**Rules.** Preview never grants or removes real permissions and is never persisted across sign-ins.

## CF-35 Consolidated Batch Ordering View (Stockist)

**Purpose.** Canvas "Weekly Batch Ordering" — plan fulfilment of many orders as one consolidated cycle.

**Actors & permissions.** Stockist Owner, Manager, Staff (read).

**Behaviour.** A planning view groups open (Pending/Accepted/Packed) orders by chosen cycle (week or scheduled delivery date or route): cycle totals (order count, value), per-pharmacy rows, and shortcuts into each order's fulfilment. It is a **view over real orders** — no separate batch entity, no bulk state changes other than the existing per-order/bulk actions it links to (accept, pack, CF-16 bulk invoicing, CF-18 route assignment).

## CF-36 Product Reference Autofill (Stockist)

**Purpose.** Canvas "Auto Fetch" / "Enhance All" product enrichment — without AI/external services.

**Behaviour.** The platform ships a small local reference list of common Indian medicines (name, brand, manufacturer, category, pack size, typical MRP, HSN, GST rate). When adding/editing a product, "Auto-fill" matches the typed name against this reference and offers to fill empty fields (never overwrites user-entered values). "Enhance all" runs the same match over catalogue rows with missing fields and reports what it filled per row.

**Rules.** Autofill suggestions are editable before save; prices are never auto-applied to existing products (price changes remain explicit — CF-20 logs them).

**Local platform equivalence.** Bundled reference dataset; no network, no AI.

## CF-37 Business Activity Log (Own Scope)

**Purpose.** Canvas stockist "Audit Logs" tile and PDD activity-history capability — a business's own trail.

**Actors & permissions.** Business Owner, Manager (`read.own` scope). Platform Admin retains the platform-wide audit log.

**Behaviour.** A read-only, filterable view of audit entries whose subject belongs to the viewing business (orders, payments, catalogue, staff, connections…): when, who, action, entity, reason. Searchable and exportable (export audited).

**Rules.** Strictly own-business scope; never shows counterparty-internal or platform-internal entries.

## CF-39 Goodwill & Advance Credit Notes

**Purpose.** Canvas manual credit note + auto "Advance CN" on overpayment — credit notes beyond the return flow.

**Actors & permissions.** Stockist Owner, Accountant (`credit.issue`).

**Behaviour.**
1. **Goodwill credit note:** issued manually to a connected pharmacy with amount and mandatory reason ("authorised adjustment"); it behaves exactly like a return-sourced credit note (applies to invoices via the standard application flow, notifies the pharmacy) and is permanently marked `source = Goodwill` with issuer + reason.
2. **Advance credit note:** when a recorded/approved payment exceeds the selected invoices' outstanding (only possible in the stockist-recorded flow, CF-13), the surplus may — with explicit confirmation — be issued as an Advance credit note (`source = Advance`, linked to the payment) instead of rejecting the payment. It applies to future invoices like any credit note.

**Rules.** Credit notes remain the only mechanism for non-payment reductions of outstanding (PDD Part 3); both variants are audited and visible to the pharmacy with their source; neither is ever created silently — advance CNs require the recorder's confirmation.

**Edge cases.** E-CF-39a: goodwill CN without a reason is blocked. E-CF-39b: advance CN cannot exceed the payment surplus.

